WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.160
It has been said that “Death is not the
greatest of evils: rather, it is to wish to

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.129
die when one cannot.”

00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:12.340
Imagine you were unable to die, never once
aging for the rest of time.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.620
Sounds like it would be pretty neat, right?

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.039
Everybody wants to live forever, but we rarely
ever think about how traumatic it would be

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:21.480
to achieve immortality.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.949
Picture all those future historical events
you would live through.

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:30.140
But think of everyone you would lose as well,
all those loved ones that would grow old and

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:36.750
pass away while you remained still, staying
exactly the same forever, frozen.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.990
If you had finite memory, it would be even
worse.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:45.820
No matter who you lost, after centuries you
would eventually forget them too, their smiles,

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:52.470
their laughs, every detail of them would be
gone from you, as you carry on living endlessly.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.880
Immortality would likely be a very lonely
path, and nobody is a better example of that

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.600
than SCP-1440, otherwise known as The Old
Man from Nowhere.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:08.740
As the nickname describes, SCP-1440 appears,
at least at first glance, to be a man of unknown

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.100
age and ethnicity.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:16.310
SCP-1440 is currently uncontained, but also
is not considered hostile or actively evil

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.990
by the SCP Foundation.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:22.060
Mostly, he spends his days wandering the wilderness
on his own.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.079
On the few instances he has crossed paths
with the Foundation, when questioned about

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:30.710
his name, or where he was born, the old man
will refuse to answer.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.579
It is not clear if this is because he does
not want to divulge personal information about

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:39.009
his origins, or if he simply doesn’t have
answers to those questions.

00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:43.119
Eyewitness accounts have described The Old
Man from Nowhere as looking like an elderly

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:45.869
gentleman, approximately eighty years old.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:51.830
However, descriptions of him have not changed
at all in the fifty years since SCP-1440’s

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:56.200
existence was first brought to the Foundation’s
attention, with him always being described

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.649
as looking the same way without changing.

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:02.240
And there’s only one conclusion we can land
on from there.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.609
SCP-1440 doesn’t age.

00:02:04.609 --> 00:02:07.540
So, you may be wondering, is that it?

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:13.900
Is SCP-1440 just an immortal wanderer, a rambling
old man who is destined to keep on living

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.420
long after all of us are dead.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.420
Not quite.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.629
In fact, that’s barely the tip of the proverbial
iceberg.

00:02:21.629 --> 00:02:26.530
Each time that The Old Man from Nowhere comes
into contact with a human population, or anything

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:30.630
man made at all, the rest of his anomalous
nature is revealed.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.560
Not instantly, since he has to remain in contact
with a population and stay close to them for

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.739
a few days.

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:41.629
Only then does this adverse effect on humanity,
and everything connected to it, become more

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:42.650
apparent.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:47.910
Should SCP-1440 dwell too close to people
and man made structures for any extended period

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:52.650
of time, massively destructive events will
begin to occur nearby.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.069
These events will continue to increase in
size and scale, until everything in the immediate

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:00.420
vicinity of the Old Man is dead and destroyed.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:07.329
Humans, buildings, vehicles, there is nothing
left around him but total and utter devastation.

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:13.370
All that survives is SCP-1440 himself, along
with the clothes on his back, a sack he carries

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:18.459
over one shoulder, a pack of playing cards,
and the small glass that he keeps on his person

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:20.410
at all times.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:26.540
Even though he causes disaster on a horrendous
scale wherever he goes, SCP-1440 is not actively

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.540
evil.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.909
The Old Man is fully aware of the effect he
has when stationed too close to civilization

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:36.440
for too long, but he doesn't create these
destructive events by choice or out of malice

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.160
for human beings.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.950
Death just seems to follow him, whether he
wants it to or not.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:47.640
And it is for exactly this reason that he
chooses a life of solitude, wandering from

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.980
place to place with the intention of avoiding
human contact for as long as he possibly can.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:04:00.220
Or at least, that’s his intention, but SCP-1440
is unable to stay away for too long.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:05.080
The Old Man from Nowhere suffers from a compulsion
to travel in a strange, highly complicated

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:10.420
pattern of movement and despite their best
efforts, the researchers of the SCP Foundation

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:15.099
have been thus far unable to properly analyze
this pattern.

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:20.370
SCP-1440 literally cannot stop himself, he
can’t even provide any useful information

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:25.430
about why he feels so compelled to travel
in such a way, most likely because he is not

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.130
even aware of it happening.

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:31.990
But whatever the reason may be, The Old Man
from Nowhere will inevitably travel in his

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:36.970
unpredictable patterns that always lead him
towards civilization, where he will come into

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:40.860
contact with people and ultimately cause their
doom.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:46.650
It is due to his unintentional, yet highly
destructive capabilities, that SCP-1440 remains

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:50.340
uncontained by the SCP Foundation to this
day.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:55.139
All previous attempts to contain him have
resulted in catastrophic losses for the Foundation,

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:58.360
both in resources and the lives of personnel.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:03.460
Even so, the Old Man is far from hostile,
and shows no contempt towards human beings.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:08.720
He will even willingly and without resistance,
allow himself to be captured and subdued whenever

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.120
the Foundation have attempted to contain him,
though he seems to know that it’s only a

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.530
matter of time before everything around him
is destroyed and he’s forced to embark on

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.030
his wandering path once again.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:26.030
SCP-1440 was first brought to the attention
of the SCP Foundation over fifty years ago.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:30.430
During a commute to work, one of the Foundation’s
research staff was approached by an old man

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.800
who appeared to be in his eighties and was
asking for her help.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:38.080
When she asked what he needed help with, the
man told her that he hoped the SCP Foundation

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.110
would be able to destroy him.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:44.600
Not only had he somehow learned the identity
of this Foundation doctor and tracked her

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:50.620
down, but SCP-1440 had sought out the Foundation
so that they could bring an end to his immortal

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.880
existence.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:53.140
Permanently.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.500
The Foundation had the Old Man from Nowhere
brought in for questioning at one of their

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.850
secret facilities - a grave mistake.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:04.919
Before they could even attempt to theorize
a way to terminate SCP-1440, as he’d requested,

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:08.620
the SCP Foundation’s site was completely
obliterated.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:13.400
Over one hundred personnel were killed, and
the loss of the facility also destroyed six

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.770
‘Safe’ and ‘Euclid’ class SCP objects.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.420
Ever since then, any attempt to contain the
Old Man from Nowhere has ended in much the

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:27.280
same way, with hundreds dead, and millions
of dollars worth of property destruction.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:32.880
Until they have a sure fire way of keeping
SCP-1440 and his destructive power contained,

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.600
their best option is to focus on observing
him from a safe distance, and trying to predict

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:40.889
his travel pattern to steer him away from
civilians.

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:46.889
But still, the Foundation has persevered with
capturing SCP-1440, even if only for brief

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:49.240
periods of time.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.620
During this time, they have conducted numerous
interviews, each time learning more and more

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.509
about the aloof, elusive immortal and his
various exploits over the centuries.

00:06:58.509 --> 00:07:02.321
Few records of these interviews have managed
to survive the destructive power of the Old

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:04.850
Man from Nowhere’s anomalous abilities.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:09.900
However, there exists one transcript, an interview
from the Foundation’s fourth attempt to

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:16.330
contain SCP-1440, that was logged and saved
to a remote server off site.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:21.169
Before the interview had begun, SCP-1440’s
arrival to the area had already started to

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:23.770
cause adverse effects on the Foundation’s
staff.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:28.440
A number of personnel reported experiencing
severe headaches and nausea.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:32.879
Over the two days that followed, many of the
site’s water purification filters were found

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:34.419
to be malfunctioning.

00:07:34.419 --> 00:07:39.150
Shortly after, a hangar at the site collapsed,
killing several Foundation airmen.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:43.250
Additionally, a member of research personnel
was found to have suffered a total collapse

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:48.590
of both kidneys and lungs simultaneously,
all despite having been in perfect physical

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:49.830
health.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:54.900
SCP-1440, complying with the Foundation as
he had before, sat down with a doctor to commence

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.060
the interview.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.770
The Old Man was quick to praise the SCP Foundation
for their continued efforts to capture and

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:05.340
contain him, even though the previous three
times had all ended catastrophically.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:10.970
He stated that he now knew the Foundation
could not help him bring an end to his immortality,

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:14.430
and that it was in their best interests to
release him.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:19.909
SCP-1440 then warned the doctor that The First
Brother was standing behind them.

00:08:19.909 --> 00:08:24.460
During previous interviews, the Old Man from
Nowhere had made similar allusions to a group

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:27.660
of brothers, three of them to be precise.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:31.030
This time, he expanded a little on who these
brothers were.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.570
“Three, Aye.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.990
Different, but one and the same.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:42.160
All cruel, all vengeful, all capable of holding
a grudge for a long time.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:48.050
They are the cause of my misfortune, and therefore
the cause of yours.”

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:52.980
It was at that moment that SCP-1440 seemed
to notice something standing behind the doctor

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:57.640
interviewing him, and warned that the Second
Brother had now joined the first.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.770
He claimed time was running out and that the
Foundation needed to release him for their

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.430
own safety before it was too late.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:08.540
The doctor politely refused, and enquired
about the Third Brother.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:13.050
SCP-1440 seemed to describe an elusive figure,
who never appeared to him.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:17.560
But, the Old Man from Nowhere seemed to imply
that one glimpse of this mysterious Third

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.950
Brother would ‘set him free’.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:25.590
Perhaps he meant by curing his tortured immortality,
or at least making it safe for SCP-1440 to

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.320
be around people without causing their destruction.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.459
“The Third never appears.

00:09:31.459 --> 00:09:36.930
In that, he is crueler than both his brothers,
for he knows his appearance is the only thing

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.650
that will set me free.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:45.670
I have spent time untold searching for him,
trying to return his prize and those I won

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:49.720
from his brothers, but to no avail.”

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:54.540
SCP-1440 remarked that the Second Brother
had his hands on the doctor’s shoulders,

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.550
taking that as an omen of doom and the doctor’s
imminent death.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:03.310
The Old Man offered one final warning:
“Should you choose to challenge Death to

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:08.640
a game of cards for your life, there is one
thing you must never do…

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.640
Win.”

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:14.300
At that precise moment, the nuclear device
kept on site as a failsafe was activated,

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.290
bypassing all security protocols and failsafes.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:21.810
The entire Foundation facility was destroyed,
killing every single member of personnel in

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.680
a quick instant of atomic obliteration.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:30.290
A week later, a figure was spotted over three
thousand kilometers away from the blast site:

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:36.220
an old man, who had suffered no apparent damage
from the explosion or the fallout.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:41.769
It seems, through his vague allusion to three
brothers and card games, that SCP-1440 gained

00:10:41.769 --> 00:10:43.910
his immortality from Death itself.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:49.430
Or rather, a group of entities known as The
Brothers Death, although they have been referred

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:56.050
to as countless names by cultures past and
present across the world; Old Gods, The All-Death,

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.900
Yulu, Yama, Kshitigarbha.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:03.209
These three brothers are a lot more than just
a trio of grim reapers collecting the souls

00:11:03.209 --> 00:11:04.209
of the dead.

00:11:04.209 --> 00:11:09.920
They are, in fact, responsible for the creation
of everything that exists as we know it, governing

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:14.980
all of reality and deciding when each part
of it must come to its unavoidable end.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:20.810
It would appear that, by challenging The Brothers
Death to a card game, SCP-1440 was cursed

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:26.220
with his eternal lifespan, while also causing
the deaths of thousands without choice or

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.220
consent.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:31.550
The items that the Old Man carries are even
the Prizes of the Brothers Death, won during

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.210
the same card game.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:38.060
While limited in their uses, they are extremely
powerful, and can reduce the Brothers’ influence

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.610
on the mortal coil.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:44.360
The glass cup holds the Elixir of Life, a
single drop capable of curing the sickest

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.639
of men and saving them from the grip of Death.

00:11:46.639 --> 00:11:51.130
The playing cards the Old Man keeps are the
Cards of Fate, holding the power to challenge

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:56.290
Death’s authority and alter fate, preventing
wars, deaths, and calamities.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:12:01.850
Finally, the Sack of the All Death, able to
carry anything within it, including unspeakable

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:05.029
catastrophes and even Death itself.

00:12:05.029 --> 00:12:10.269
As human populations spread further into previously
uninhabited areas, it’s becoming harder

00:12:10.269 --> 00:12:14.130
for SCP-1440 to avoid contact with people.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:19.590
Drawn to them by his unstoppable compulsion,
he continues to live out century after century

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:23.740
spent causing destruction and death wherever
he wanders to.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:28.050
Just pray that the old man never finds his
way to your town…

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:35.430
No go check out “SCP-1879 - Indoor Salesman”
and “SCP-2852 Sadistic Madman Party Crasher

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:39.300
| Cousin Johnny” for more strange men you
really don’t want to run into!

